    <edge source="api" target="who gmp guidelines" id="1">
      <data key="d7">GOVERNED_BY</data>
      <data key="d8">9</data>
      <data key="d9">["WHO good manufacturing practices: starting materials", "6.53 Written procedures should be established and followed for investigating critical deviations or the failure of a batch of intermediate or API to meet specifications.", "Batch production and laboratory control records of critical process steps should be reviewed and approved by the quality unit(s) before an API batch is released or distributed.", "Where appropriate, the stability storage conditions should be consistent with the WHO guidelines on stability.", "An API expiry or retest date should be based on an evaluation of data derived from stability studies.", "For each batch of intermediate and API, appropriate laboratory tests should be conducted to determine conformance to specifications.", "Equipment cleaning or sanitization studies should address microbiological and endotoxin contamination for those processes where there is a need to reduce total microbiological count or endotoxins in the API", "Where the quality of the API can be affected by microbial contamination, manipulations using open vessels should be performed in a biosafety cabinet or similarly controlled environment.", "These guidelines apply to new and existing APIs ..."]</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk_7573..chunk_7575, chunk_7606..chunk_7608, chunk_7609..chunk_7611, chunk_7639..chunk_7641, chunk_7633..chunk_7635, chunk_7651..chunk_7653, chunk_7675..chunk_7677, chunk_8917..chunk_8919</data>
      <data key="d11">who_gmp_guidelines.md</data>
    </edge>
