    </edge>
    <edge source="operational qualification" target="who good manufacturing practices" id="0">
      <data key="d7">STANDARDIZED_UNDER</data>
      <data key="d8">4</data>
      <data key="d9">["Documented verification that the system or subsystem operates as intended over all anticipated operating ranges.", "design qualification (DQ), a factory acceptance test (FAT), site acceptance test (SAT), installation qualification (IQ), operational qualification (OQ) and performance qualification (PQ).", "Chunk chunk_7213: 10.19 OQ should provide documented evidence that utilities, systems or equipment operate in accordance with operational specifications.", "operational qualification. This is the documentary evidence to verify that the equipment operates in accordance with its design specifications within its normal operating range and performs as intended throughout all anticipated operating ranges."]</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk_7195..chunk_7197, chunk_7210..chunk_7212, chunk_7213..chunk_7215, chunk_7486..chunk_7488</data>
      <data key="d11">who_gmp_guidelines.md</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="operational qualification" target="who gmp guidelines" id="0">
      <data key="d7">STANDARDIZED_UNDER</data>
      <data key="d8">2</data>
      <data key="d9">["The OQ \u2013 or operational/functional verification testing \u2013 should provide documented evidence that software and hardware function as intended over anticipated operating ranges.", "Appropriate installation qualification and operational qualification should demonstrate the suitability of computer hardware and software to perform assigned tasks."]</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk_7303..chunk_7305, chunk_7594..chunk_7596</data>
      <data key="d11">who_gmp_guidelines.md</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="performance qualification" target="who good manufacturing practices" id="0">
      <data key="d7">STANDARDIZED_UNDER</data>
      <data key="d8">4</data>
      <data key="d9">["Documented verification that the equipment or system performs consistently and reproducibly within defined specifications and parameters in its normal operating environment (i.e. in the production environment).", "design qualification (DQ), a factory acceptance test (FAT), site acceptance test (SAT), installation qualification (IQ), operational qualification (OQ) and performance qualification (PQ).", "Chunk chunk_7214: 10.23 Normally, PQ should be conducted prior to release of the utilities, systems or equipment.", "performance qualification. The documented verification that the process and/ or the total process related to the system performs as intended throughout all anticipated operating ranges."]</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk_7195..chunk_7197, chunk_7210..chunk_7212, chunk_7213..chunk_7215, chunk_7486..chunk_7488</data>
      <data key="d11">who_gmp_guidelines.md</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="performance qualification" target="who gmp guidelines" id="0">
      <data key="d7">STANDARDIZED_UNDER</data>
      <data key="d8">3</data>
      <data key="d9">["12.1 PQ, which includes UAT, should be conducted to verify the intended system use and administration defined in the URS and DQ, or equivalent document.", "performance qualification should be carried out and fully documented.", "Laboratory equipment should undergo design qualification, installation qualification, operation qualification and performance qualification (chunk_9737)"]</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk_7303..chunk_7305, chunk_8179..chunk_8181, chunk_9736..chunk_9738</data>
      <data key="d11">who_gmp_guidelines.md</data>
    </edge>
